AmiXnet Regulations and Standards as of 21 May 93


   Welcome to AmiXnet, we hope through the efforts of all involved that
   we make this the most user friendly netmailing system around.

   The Following information (Regulations and Standards) is by no means
   complete. I am sure there will be updates etc. But for now, Our 
   primary goal is to establish some standards of adherence to the net.
   These standards must be maintained by all users of the net , including
   the Sysop.
 
   
   1.> The Host of a News Group or Conference should make available
       a description of there News Group, and establish guidelines
       which he/she expects to be maintained, that are not otherwise
       mentioned in this document.

   2.> Foul Language is prohibited unless the HOST of the conference
       states otherwise.
 
       unless otherwise stated in the guidelines from the HOST, any
       violation of this could result in loss of access for the user
       to that particular news group, and even loss of the news group
       for that node.  

   3.> News Groups must be respected by both the sysop and the user. 
       Some News Groups require REAL NAMES, and Some Allow alias's

       Some may not be used to using REAL NAMES on a BBS. If this is the
       case, then we respectively request you use a ficticious name.
       This means a First and Last Name.

       unless otherwise stated in the guidelines from the HOST, any
       violation of this could result in loss of access for the user
       to that particular news group, and even loss of the news group
       for that node.  

   4.> Currently the mailroute should be strictly followed. If you are not
       sure how to transfer mail from one node to another, then please
       let the TERM door do all of this for you. The logic and implementation
       of the AmiXnet does not permit jumping nodes at this time. 
       Jumping/Hopping nodes with the mail transfers can result in duplicate
       mail.
 
   5.> Some News Groups may require a subscription fee. The fee is at the
       discretion of the host. I highly suggest that any fee be in the
       form of monthly donations or annual donations, and if your news group
       does accept donatations then kindly share the wealth with the author
       of the AmiXnet mail system ;).

       Seriously, if a host wishes a subscription fee, then I highly suggest
       the Host do his/her home work on the legalities of such a venture.
       I believe a donation based News Group is the safest and most friendly.
 
   6.> Each node in the AmiXnet system must carry the AX0001 AmiXnet Info
       News Group conference. Currently this is a free News Group which
       is the primary channel of communication with the net administrator.
       The Net administration will be responsible for assigning node-ids
       and also responsible for the overseeing the complete net operations.
       He/She will handle any disputes or problems within the net
       administration.
 
   7.> Hosts are responsibile for maintaining the mailroute for his/her
       newsgroup. THIS IS NOT THE RESPONSIBILITY of the NET ADMINISTRATOR.
 
       If as a host you are unclear of the procedures to do such a thing
       please request information from the Net Administrator on proper
       procedures for implementation.

   8.> Node assignements should be requested to the Net Administrator:
       Chris Kawchuk@416001 in the AX0001 conference. He will need to
       know which news groups you want, and also he will need to know
       the positioning in the mailroute for you to pickup mail. If you
       are unsure of this procedure, please consult the node you plan
       on obtaining mail from.

   9.> I highly suggest that BRANCHES in the NET not exceed 5 LEAVES/BUDS.

  10.> LOGNET Passwords shall be assigned by the Sysop of the node in which
       you will be receiving mail.

